{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1530 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "16694042ad6b7755ed1df904ed53019c6cd2fcb6350c90a15f3262ee0d56523d" :edb/db-before-t 1529 :edb/db-after-t 1530 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534842 50 #inst "2026-10-12T21:57:34.991Z" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186118628 1078 #edb/ref 17592186118632 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119687 1071 "Calculate the value of \n![](images/1f/1fd9cafe0db4412b48885cebacd68b9866a79fadfdb7767c3b63f8469d31bfea.svg)\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of $a_{31}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\times 4$ determinant to a $3 \\times 3$ determinant.*" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119687 1071 "Calculate the value of \n![](images/9c/9cb26049b5e3d06f9ef9e07ce617042166330b1eddb84063d7970799ebf6d8e5.png)\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of $a_{31}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\times 4$ determinant to a $3 \\times 3$ determinant.*" 13194139534842 17592186045417 false] [17592186119870 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440778 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119870 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440781 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119874 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440776 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119874 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440777 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119874 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440779 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119874 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440782 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119875 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440780 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186119995 1050 840.0 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186120419 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186120419 1071 "Calculate the value of\n$\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}$.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below $a_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\cdot 4$ determinant to a $3 \\cdot 3$ determinant.*" 13194139534842 17592186045417 false] [17592186120419 1071 "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186120419 1074 "Using elementary row operations, let's make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-(-2)) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186120547 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119395 13194139534842 17592186045417 false] [17592186121046 1064 "One way to simplify a determinant calculation is to create a row (or column) containing all zeros except for one entry. Then, we can use a Laplace expansion across that row (or column) to compute the determinant.\n\nLet's demonstrate this method on the matrix $A$ below.\n\n![](images/37/37946204f088b803603ba8adc3f93494e1d49fbe59d9c0925347675311b23e5d.svg)\n\nNotice that we can make entries to the right of $a_{21}=1$ equal to zero using elementary *column* operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one column to another column in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 14 & 17\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(21-10) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186121046 1064 "One way to simplify a determinant calculation is to create a row (or column) containing all zeros except for one entry. Then, we can use a Laplace expansion across that row (or column) to compute the determinant.\n\nLet's demonstrate this method on the matrix $A$ below.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 14 & 17\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNotice that we can make entries to the right of $a_{21}=1$ equal to zero using elementary *column* operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one column to another column in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 14 & 17\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(21-10) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534842 17592186045417 false] [17592186440734 1080 "4" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440734 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440734 1083 #uuid "077a1997-2530-5fe1-b114-aa83cbfd33fd" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440735 1080 "11" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440735 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440735 1083 #uuid "15adda79-ba8c-5250-86b2-2c890fbe9191" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440736 1080 "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -2\\end{aligned}|" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440736 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440736 1083 #uuid "24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440737 1080 "-2|\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 10 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}|" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440737 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440737 1083 #uuid "333b186d-9fdb-5337-9547-777d95fd43a9" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440738 1080 "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440738 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440738 1083 #uuid "45d716cf-9dbc-5925-a952-39f8a779d625" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440739 1080 "-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 13 & 1\\end{aligned}|" 13194139534842 17592186045417 true] [17592186440739 1082 #edb/ref 17592186